Method References (::)
----------------------

A method reference is a shorter way of writing a lambda expression when the lambda simply calls an existing method

Using Lambda: `x -> x.toUpperCase()`
Using Method Reference: `String::toUpperCase`

There are four main types:
Type	                                Example
Static method reference	                ClassName::staticMethod
Instance method reference           	object::instanceMethod
Instance method of an arbitrary object	ClassName::instanceMethod
Constructor reference	                ClassName::new


Lambda              	        Method Reference
Uses ->	Uses                     ::
Can contain logic	            Refers to an existing method
More flexible	                Shorter and cleaner
Can call multiple methods	    Usually delegates to one method


Every lambda expression cannot be converted into a method reference.
A lambda can be converted into a method reference only when it simply calls an existing method or constructor and the method reference matches the required functional interface